source: tests/snapshots.rs
expression: help_for(&args)
---
Create a new payment link (POST /v2/payment-links)

Usage: flute2 payment-links create [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --card-enabled
          Accept card payments. At least one payment method is required
      --card-processor-id <CARD_PROCESSOR_ID>
          Charge card payments through this processor
      --ach-enabled
          Accept ACH payments
      --ach-processor-id <ACH_PROCESSOR_ID>
          Charge ACH payments through this processor
      --amount <AMOUNT>
          Amount to collect. Plain decimal, e.g. `100.00`. Omit for a link the payer fills in
      --currency-code <CURRENCY_CODE>
          Currency code, e.g. `USD` (required)
      --link-type <LINK_TYPE>
          Link type: `single-use` (default) or `multi-use` [possible values: multi-use, single-use]
      --customer-id <CUSTOMER_ID>
          Customer UUID to issue the link for
      --reference-id <REFERENCE_ID>
          Merchant-assigned reference ID
      --name <NAME>
          Merchant-facing label for the link
      --description <DESCRIPTION>
          Merchant-internal notes. Never shown to customers
      --expires-on <EXPIRES_ON>
          UTC expiry (ISO 8601, ending in `Z`), e.g. `2026-09-15T00:00:00Z`. Omit for a link that never expires
  -h, --help
          Print help

Global options:
      --profile <PROFILE>  Active profile (environment). `sandbox` (default) or `production`/`prod` [env: FLUTE2_PROFILE=]
      --output <OUTPUT>    Output format: table (default), json, or quiet (id only). When omitted, falls back to the `FLUTE2_OUTPUT` env var, then to the `output` key in ~/.flute2/config.toml, then to `table` [env: FLUTE2_OUTPUT=] [possible values: table, json, quiet]
      --debug              Print HTTP request/response traces to stderr. Card and bank-account numbers are masked to the last 4 digits; CVV/security codes are removed
